    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "mNPZa",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2400,
      "name": "Direction B — Focus, no chrome",
      "fill": "#08090B",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 48,
      "padding": 80,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "FYaPg",
          "name": "Direction header",
          "width": 1100,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 10,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Zvlv7",
              "name": "Tag",
              "fill": "$accent",
              "content": "DIRECTION B",
              "fontFamily": "$mono",
              "fontSize": 13,
              "fontWeight": "normal",
              "letterSpacing": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Zpj4s",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$fg",
              "content": "Focus mode: no sidebar, palette is the navigation",
              "fontFamily": "$font",
              "fontSize": 36,
              "fontWeight": "600",
              "letterSpacing": -0.5
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "eb04d",
              "name": "Description",
              "fill": "$fg-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Superhuman-style. There is no sidebar: the whole width goes to one dense, single-line list, and you move between places with ⌘K or g-chords (g m: my work, g p: project). My work is a split inbox sorted by why it needs you, and the reason is the first column. An opened item takes the full screen with j / k to step through. A bar at the bottom always shows the keys for the current selection, plus sync and API state. Issues and PRs stay separate rows, linked visibly. Projects default to a board.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
