              "type": "text",
              "id": "fLZQw",
              "name": "Description",
              "fill": "$fg-2",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "A triage desk. A thin icon rail replaces the sidebar. My work is three side-by-side lanes (Your move, Waiting on others, Assigned), so you see all of it at once, and ← → jumps between lanes. Opening an item is a peek: a sheet floats over the lanes, j / k steps through without closing it, Esc returns. Projects are a calm table: the project's own fields become columns, rows are grouped by any field (here Iteration: current, next, past), and cells are edited in place.",
