                              "name": "Caption note",
                              "fill": "$fg-2",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": "fill_container",
                              "content": "Picking vitejs/vite brings its templates in before the user writes more than a title. The user can't push to vite, so its issue forms aren't filled in githq: the row says “form on GitHub”, and Enter opens GitHub's own form with the title carried over in the URL. GitHub would drop a form's labels and skip its required-field check for an issue created through the API by a non-maintainer. The markdown template is still filled in here. Blank issues are turned off, so that row says so instead of disappearing.",
