                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "id": "jcgKG",
                              "name": "Description",
                              "fill": "$fg-2",
                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                              "width": 1200,
                              "content": "One thin bar along the bottom of the window, split into a segment under each surface: sidebar, list, item. Each segment says in dim text what its surface shows (“Up to date”). When something is off, that segment takes the colour and says what and since when. Always in the same place, so the eye learns where to look, and the list and the item can visibly disagree.",
